FDWM's own, after bakkeby's version of upstream's swallow patch
(https://dwm.suckless.org/patches/swallow/, dwm-swallow-6.5.diff in
https://github.com/bakkeby/patches): a window started from a terminal
takes the terminal's place in the client and focus lists (replaceclient())
until it closes, rather than the two windows swapping. Rules gain
isterminal and noswallow; st (class st-256color) is a terminal, the rules
after it for the scratchpads and fdwm-theme-menu's st turn that off, and
xev's window never swallows. A window's process comes from the X-Resource
extension through xcb-res (config.mk links it) and its parents from
/proc/PID/stat, read past the last ")" since a command name can hold
spaces; Linux only, so the patch's OpenBSD code is left out, and so is its
swterminheritfs (a terminal coming back never takes its program's
fullscreen). Unlike the patch: alwayscenter doesn't recenter a window in a
floating terminal's place, and scan() manages the terminals before the
other windows, so after a restart a program that had swallowed its
terminal finds it and swallows it again.

